{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3639770","formula":"C₄₆H₅₆N₁₀O₁₀","hill":"C46H56N10O10","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":46.0,"H":56.0,"N":10.0,"O":10.0},"names":{"en":"Biphalin"},"descriptions":{"en":"Biphalin is a dimeric enkephalin endogenous peptide (Tyr-D-Ala-Gly-Phe-NH)2 composed of two tetrapeptides derived from enkephalins, connected 'tail-to-tail' by a hydrazide bridge. The presence of two distinct pharmacophores confers on biphalin a high affinity for both μ and δ opioid receptors (with an EC50 of about 1–5 nM for both μ and δ receptors), therefore it has analgesic activity. Biphalin presents a considerable antinociceptive profile."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":5487663,"mass":909.0,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@H](C(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](CC1=CC=CC=C1)C(=O)NNC(=O)[C@H](CC2=CC=CC=C2)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H](C)NC(=O)[C@H](CC3=CC=C(C=C3)O)N)NC(=O)[C@H](CC4=CC=C(C=C4)O)N","inchikey":"DESSEGDLRYOPTJ-VRANXALZSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-amino-N-[(2R)-1-[[2-[[(2S)-1-[2-[(2S)-2-[[2-[[(2R)-2-[[(2S)-2-amino-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)propanoyl]amino]propanoyl]amino]acetyl]amino]-3-phenylpropanoyl]hydrazinyl]-1-oxo-3-phenylpropan-2-yl]amino]-2-oxoethyl]amino]-1-oxopropan-2-yl]-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)propanamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"5487663","atoms":122,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.98,"y":4.512,"z":-3.472,"el":"C"},{"x":1.706,"y":3.689,"z":-2.223,"el":"C"},{"x":2.461,"y":2.347,"z":-2.309,"el":"C"},{"x":2.011,"y":1.353,"z":-2.877,"el":"O"},{"x":3.7,"y":2.373,"z":-1.704,"el":"N"},{"x":4.519,"y":1.179,"z":-1.554,"el":"C"},{"x":4.475,"y":0.617,"z":-0.129,"el":"C"},{"x":5.393,"y":-0.057,"z":0.333,"el":"O"},{"x":3.307,"y":0.847,"z":0.56,"el":"N"},{"x":3.222,"y":0.642,"z":2.008,"el":"C"},{"x":3.958,"y":1.731,"z":2.816,"el":"C"},{"x":3.859,"y":3.